     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"answer\":\"The current recall match rests on the owner's reported ICCU failure and inability to accelerate, matching recall 24V868000's loss-of-drive-power description. Evidence of a different model year or a different cause of the failure would warrant re-checking recall coverage and that match, rather than changing the decision here. Repair history is not in these records; it would be needed to assess whether the vehicle had not received the recall repair or had failed after repair.\",\"scope\":\"answered\",\"recheck\":false,\"citations\":[{\"kind\":\"complaint\",\"id\":\"11714455\",\"quote\":\"they said it is an ICCU failure\"},{\"kind\":\"complaint\",\"id\":\"11714455\",\"quote\":\"Car would not accelerate\"},{\"kind\":\"recall\",\"id\":\"24V868000\",\"quote\":\"which can result in a loss of drive power\"},{\"kind\":\"recall\",\"id\":\"24V868000\",\"quote\":\"Hyundai Motor America (Hyundai) is recalling certain 2022-2024 IONIQ 5\"}]}",
